PATCH 510: the radio-message and compass cockpit cells 842d / 8463.

Two more 209e paint methods.  BX is the display-list element's DGROUP NEAR OFFSET (published to
DGROUP:0x3e08 by the walk) and BP the walk base (g_fist_paintbp, patch 142); both were dereferenced as
host pointers and the WORD [bx+2] read as a 4-byte int.

FUN_1000_842d (asm 0x1842d-0x18462):
    1842d: mov si,[bx+2] ; movb [bp+si],3
    18433: mov al,[0x1548] ; or al,al ; je 0x18450 ; js 0x1843d ; lret
    1843d: and al,0x7f ; cmp al,3 ; jne 0x1844f
    18443: mov bx,0x8fc4 ; lcall [0x694] ; movb [0x1548],0
    18450: testw [0x6d16],1 ; je 0x1844f ; call 0x1a8d7 ; movw [0x1552],0x8fc4
The BX=0x8fc4 argument of the [0x694] far call was dropped.

FUN_1000_8463 (asm 0x18463-0x184c2), its sibling, adds two more defects: DAT_2000_2d34 -- the PLAYER's
NEAR OFFSET -- dereferenced as a host pointer, and the `mov gs,[0x70]` STRING-SEGMENT base of the
compass table dropped, so Ghidra read `[bx+0x253a]` at the bare host address 0x253a:
    1848c: mov ax,[di+0x89] ; add ax,0x400 ; mov bl,ah ; and bx,0xf8 ; shr bx,1 ; shr bx,1
    1849d: mov gs,[0x70] ; mov ax,gs:[bx+0x253a] ; mov [0x1550],ax ; movw [0x1552],0x8fa8

842d was the top SIGSEGV of the post-509 sweep (842d <- 7f53 <- 209e <- 206f <- 459a).
